## What this directory is

The stock dadi cache integration (dadi/DFE/Cache1D_mod.py, method Cache1D.integrate)
computes the two EXTERIOR tail weights with scipy.integrate.quad:

    weight_neu, err_neu = scipy.integrate.quad(sel_dist, 0, -smallest_gamma, args=params)
    weight_del, err     = scipy.integrate.quad(sel_dist, -largest_gamma, np.inf, args=params)

upstream comment: "Not using CDF function because want this to be able to compute
weight for arbitrary mass functions". The interior of the sampled gamma range is not
integrated by quad at all — it is np.trapz over the cached spectra.

The patch here replaces those two quad calls with closed-form gamma CDF expressions
for the gamma and neugamma pdfs, because quad loses accuracy when the scale parameter
is very small (the pdf becomes a narrow spike that adaptive quadrature can step over).

The patch is NOT active in the pipeline. Stock quad is what the package uses.

